# Banked bench outputs — a machine-local cache keyed by content hash, and bulk
# model prose besides. The verdicts and their cited rationale live in the
# committed tests/bench/battles.jsonl; commit these too if cross-machine
# re-judging ever becomes a thing worth paying git weight for.
tests/bench/outputs/

# OpenSpec's per-tool skill copies. `openspec init plans/development` writes
# the same six workflows twice for every tool it targets: once as a skill and
# once as a slash command. The commands are committed and are what the workflow
# is actually driven through; these skill duplicates are regenerable and were
# only bulk. Run that init to get them back.
# Deliberately narrow: .claude/skills/two-store-memory-setup is a symlink into
# skills/ and must stay tracked, so this cannot be a blanket .claude/skills/.
.agents/skills/
.claude/skills/openspec-*/
.gemini/skills/
.opencode/skills/
